1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
And I can use an analogy here.

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:04,100
Imagine you're standing on a very calm day

3
00:00:04,520 --> 00:00:06,860
in front of a very crystal clear pool,

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:09,620
and you throw a penny to the bottom of the pool.

5
00:00:11,170 --> 00:00:13,330
Now, you can't really see the water

6
00:00:13,330 --> 00:00:14,970
because it's crystal clear,

7
00:00:15,570 --> 00:00:17,770
but you can see the penny at the bottom of the pool

8
00:00:17,770 --> 00:00:19,190
and anyone who's done this

9
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:22,190
knows that you see a distorted view of that penny.

10
00:00:22,350 --> 00:00:24,850
It doesn't appear as it would just on the ground.

11
00:00:25,210 --> 00:00:26,930
And that's because the light from the penny

12
00:00:26,930 --> 00:00:28,470
is traveling through the water

13
00:00:28,470 --> 00:00:30,530
and the light is bent by the water.

14
00:00:31,130 --> 00:00:32,190
So in this analogy,

15
00:00:32,550 --> 00:00:34,690
that penny is like the distant galaxy

16
00:00:35,210 --> 00:00:38,290
and the water is like the dark matter.

17
00:00:38,630 --> 00:00:40,330
So we don't actually see the dark matter.

18
00:00:40,510 --> 00:00:41,590
You don't actually see the water,

19
00:00:41,930 --> 00:00:43,230
but you know it's there.

20
00:00:43,610 --> 00:00:44,570
You know the water is there

21
00:00:44,570 --> 00:00:46,710
because you see a distorted view of the penny.

22
00:00:47,090 --> 00:00:48,370
And we know the dark matter is there

23
00:00:48,370 --> 00:00:50,010
because we see a distorted image

24
00:00:50,010 --> 00:00:51,330
of these background galaxies.

